11. Check Cluster Version
Command:
oc version
Example output:
Client Version: 4.18.6
Server Version: 4.18.6
Kubernetes Version: v1.31.6
Meaning
Field	Meaning
Client Version	CLI version
Server Version	OpenShift version
Kubernetes Version	underlying Kubernetes
________________________________________
12. View Cluster Information
Command:
oc cluster-info
Output:
Kubernetes control plane is running at
https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
Meaning
Shows:
•	API server address
•	cluster endpoints
Used for:
cluster debugging
________________________________________
13. List Supported API Versions
Command:
oc api-versions
Example:
apps/v1
admissionregistration.k8s.io/v1
apps.openshift.io/v1
Purpose
Shows API groups supported by cluster.
Kubernetes resources are organized as:
group/version
Example:
apps/v1
________________________________________
14. List Cluster Operators
Command:
oc get clusteroperator
Example output:
authentication
console
dns
etcd
ingress
image-registry
What are Cluster Operators?
Cluster operators manage core components of OpenShift.
Examples:
Operator	Function
authentication	login system
dns	DNS services
etcd	cluster database
ingress	external routing
image-registry	container image storage
________________________________________
15. View Pods in System Project
Command:
oc get pods -n openshift-apiserver
Explanation
Part	Meaning
oc	OpenShift CLI
get pods	list pods
-n	specify namespace
Example output:
apiserver-68c9485699
This pod runs the API server.
________________________________________
16. Check Project Status
Command:
oc status -n openshift-authentication
Purpose
Provides high-level overview of project resources.
Shows:
•	deployments
•	services
•	routes
•	pods
Example:
deployment/oauth-openshift
This service handles authentication.
________________________________________
17. View Resource Documentation
Command:
oc explain services
Purpose
Shows resource structure.
Example fields:
apiVersion
metadata
spec
status
This helps when writing YAML files.
________________________________________
18. List Cluster Nodes
Command:
oc get nodes
Example output:
NAME       STATUS   ROLES
master01   Ready    control-plane,master,worker
Meaning
Cluster contains:
1 node
This node acts as:
•	master
•	control-plane
•	worker
________________________________________
19. Finish the Lab
Command:
lab finish cli-interfaces
Purpose
This cleans up:
•	temporary resources
•	lab configurations
Prevents interference with next exercises.
